Tasks: default

Purpose:
  Manage executable work generated from prompts, analysis,
  decisions and project changes. Define task contracts,
  decomposition rules, dependency types, granularity guidelines,
  and coverage requirements.

Owns: ./

  Scope:
    Task definition and contract
    Task lifecycle and state
    Task decomposition engine
    Dependency types and DAG enforcement
    Task granularity and atomicity
    Task scope boundaries
    Acceptance criteria
    Task coverage matrix
    Scope expansion protocol
    Plan versioning
    SDD pyramid branching hierarchy
    Branch naming and merge flow
    Branch lifecycle and deletion policy
    Commit message format and decision/task linkage

Principles:
  Task is specification, not execution.
  Task = Goal + Scope + Input + Dependencies + Acceptance + Output.
  Task MUST be atomic, not implementation-detail-level.
  Task graph MUST be a DAG.
  AI proposes tasks; engine validates structure.
  Acceptance criteria are behavioral, not implementation.

Lifecycle:
  DISCOVERING -> PLANNING -> IMPLEMENTING -> TESTING -> REVIEWING -> COMPLETED
                                    |
                                    +-> FIXING -> TESTING (iterative loop, bounded)
                                    +-> DOCUMENTING -> LEARNING -> COMPLETED
                                    +-> BLOCKED
                                    +-> ESCALATED

  Legacy state mapping (6-state -> 10-state):
    DRAFT      -> DISCOVERING
    READY      -> PLANNING
    IN_PROGRESS -> IMPLEMENTING
    BLOCKED    -> BLOCKED
    DONE       -> COMPLETED
    CANCELLED  -> ESCALATED
    FAILED     -> execution sub-state within FIXING loop (not a top-level task state)

  State definitions:
    DISCOVERING: Task intent is being clarified; context is being loaded.
    PLANNING: Implementation plan is being created; constraints are verified.
    IMPLEMENTING: Code changes are being made per the plan.
    TESTING: Automated and manual tests are being executed.
    REVIEWING: Human review of implementation and tests is pending.
    FIXING: Implementation or tests failed; agent is analyzing and correcting.
    DOCUMENTING: Code is complete; documentation and API specs are being generated.
    LEARNING: Knowledge gate is being evaluated; consolidation pipeline runs.
    COMPLETED: All criteria met, done-proof verified, knowledge consolidated.
    BLOCKED: External dependency or decision is pending; task is suspended.
    ESCALATED: Human intervention is required; autonomy ceiling reached.

  FailureClassification:
    BUILD_FAILURE: compilation, dependency, or build pipeline failure
    TEST_FAILURE: automated test did not pass
    LOGIC_FAILURE: code runs but behavior is incorrect
    ARCHITECTURE_FAILURE: design or structural violation detected
    CONSTRAINT_FAILURE: policy, security, or architectural constraint violated
    ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE: infrastructure, dependency, or runtime unavailability
    KNOWLEDGE_GAP: insufficient knowledge to proceed without retrieval
    AMBIGUITY: task specification is unclear; requires human clarification
    EXTERNAL_DEPENDENCY: third-party service or external system failure

LoopProtection:
  loop_score:
    definition: cumulative risk score for the current FIXING loop
    increments:
      same_action: +30 (agent repeated an unchanged action)
      same_error: +25 (same error recurred after fix attempt)
      no_progress: +30 (no measurable change between iterations)
      plan_reverted: +20 (plan was rolled back to a prior version)
    decrements:
      new_evidence: -20 (new knowledge was retrieved)
      meaningful_change: -30 (structural change with evidence of progress)
    threshold: >= 60 triggers LOOP_RISK_HIGH
    action_on_high: task is BLOCKED and human is notified

  failure_budget:
    definition: remaining allowable failure iterations per task
    default: 3
    action_on_exhausted: task is ESCALATED to human
    reset_on_meaningful_change: +1 budget when meaningful_change decrement applies
    scope: per FIXING loop; resets on transition to new top-level state

  autonomy_level:
    L0: observe-only — AI reports findings, human decides all actions
    L1: human-approved actions — AI proposes, human approves each step
    L2: autonomous within approved plan — AI executes, human reviews per gate
    L3: autonomous with checkpoints — AI executes, human reviews at milestones
    L4: autonomous with notification — AI executes, human is informed of outcomes
    L5: fully autonomous — AI executes, documents, and learns without human gate
    default: L2
    policy_override: domain-specific autonomy caps defined in @../runtime/context-policy.sdd

TaskMemory:
  scope: per-task working state loaded during execution
  source: @../runtime/memory-model.sdd (4-tier model: Long-Term -> Project -> Task -> Working)
  context_builder: @../runtime/context-builder.sdd (task -> project -> module -> domain -> dependencies)
  context_policy: @../runtime/context-policy.sdd (always_load allowlist, negative knowledge, DO NOT registry)
  context_manifest: @../runtime/context-manifest.sdd (loaded:, excluded:, context_confidence:, missed:)
  consolidation: @../runtime/memory-consolidation.sdd (end-of-task: DROP | ARCHIVE | LINK | PROMOTE)
  rule: task memory is runtime-only — not persisted to .sdd/
  rule: context budget defaults to Level 0-1-2; expand to 3-4 on demand (PHASE 123 §10)
  rule: context sufficiency check (confidence rating) MUST pass before implementation begins

TaskContract:
  structure:
    id: string (immutable, e.g. TASK-AUTH-001)
    title: string
    type: string (FEATURE, BUGFIX, REFACTOR, MIGRATION, TEST, DOCUMENTATION, SECURITY, INFRASTRUCTURE, RESEARCH, DISCOVERY, DESIGN, DECISION, IMPLEMENTATION, REVIEW, VALIDATION, CLEANUP)
    domain: string
    goal: string
    scope:
      allowed: [paths]
      forbidden: [paths]
    inputs:
      - API-AUTH-LOGIN
    dependencies:
      - TASK-AUTH-000
    skills:
      - SKILL-API-IMPLEMENT
    acceptance:
      - valid credentials return token
      - invalid credentials return 401
    outputs:
      - source_code
      - tests
    estimated: duration
    risk: low | medium | high | critical
    boundary:
      MUST_CHANGE: [paths that must be modified]
      MAY_CHANGE: [paths that may be modified]
      MUST_NOT_CHANGE: [paths that must not be touched]
    proof:
      - unit-test
      - integration-test
      - architecture-check

TaskTypes:
  FEATURE:
    purpose: new capability
    outputs: code, tests, docs

  BUGFIX:
    purpose: fix defect
    outputs: fix, regression test

  REFACTOR:
    purpose: improve structure without behavior change
    outputs: refactored code, same tests

  MIGRATION:
    purpose: data or schema change
    outputs: migration, rollback, verification

  TEST:
    purpose: testing work
    outputs: tests, reports

  DOCUMENTATION:
    purpose: documentation
    outputs: docs

  SECURITY:
    purpose: security improvement
    outputs: fix, test, policy update

  INFRASTRUCTURE:
    purpose: infra change
    outputs: config, script, verification

  RESEARCH:
    purpose: analysis and decision
    outputs: decision document, not code

TaskGranularity:
  levels:
    EPIC:
      description: large initiative
      decomposes_to: FEATURE

    FEATURE:
      description: capability
      decomposes_to: TASK

    TASK:
      description: single goal, defined scope
      decomposes_to: SUBTASK (only when necessary)

    SUBTASK:
      description: implementation detail
      rule: MUST NOT be created unless truly necessary

  anti_patterns:
    too_large:
      description: "Build entire payment system"
      rule: decompose to atomic tasks

    too_small:
      description: "Create file", "Add import"
      rule: these are implementation details, not tasks

DependencyTypes:
  BLOCKING:
    definition: task cannot start until dependency completes
    example: database migration before repository implementation

  NON_BLOCKING:
    definition: informational dependency, task can start
    example: documentation dependency

  DATA:
    definition: task requires output artifact of dependency
    example: migration produces schema, repository requires schema

  CONTRACT:
    definition: task requires contract stability, not implementation
    example: frontend can mock API before backend completes

  RESOURCE:
    definition: task requires shared resource
    example: deployment window, environment

  SEQUENCE:
    definition: ordered execution for correctness
    example: security review after implementation

DependencyGraph:
  rule: MUST be DAG (Directed Acyclic Graph)
  rule: cycle detection MUST happen at validation time
  rule: parallel tasks MUST have no blocking dependencies between them
  rule: critical path MUST be identifiable

AIProposal:
  responsibilities:
    - understanding requirement
    - proposing decomposition
    - proposing dependencies
    - proposing acceptance criteria
    - proposing skill mappings

  limitations:
    - DOES NOT validate structure
    - DOES NOT enforce constraints
    - DOES NOT authorize changes
    - DOES NOT schedule execution

EngineValidation:
  responsibilities:
    - coverage validation
    - cycle detection
    - schema validation
    - policy validation
    - permission checking
    - scheduling

  rule: engine is source of truth for correctness

AIVsEngine:
  | Task                    | AI | Engine |
  | ----------------------- | -: | -----: |
  | Requirement understanding |  ? |      ? |
  | Task proposal           |  ? |      ? |
  | Dependency proposal     |  ? |      ? |
  | Coverage                | ?? |      ? |
  | Cycle detection         |  ? |      ? |
  | Schema validation       |  ? |      ? |
  | Policy validation       |  ? |      ? |
  | Permission              |  ? |      ? |
  | Scheduling              | ?? |      ? |

CoverageMatrix:
  structure:
    | Requirement      | Tasks    | Tests  |
    | ---------------- | -------- | ------ |
    | Reset password   | T1,T2,T3 | TEST-1 |
    | Send email       | T4       | TEST-2 |
    | Token expiration | T1       | TEST-3 |

  rule: every requirement MUST map to at least one task
  rule: incomplete coverage MUST produce INCOMPLETE_COVERAGE error

OrphanTask:
  definition: task with no requirement link

  allowed_types:
    - technical debt
    - refactoring
    - maintenance
    - infrastructure

  rule: orphan tasks MUST have explicit type justification

DynamicTaskGraph:
  principle: task plan is NOT immutable

  PLAN
   ?
  DISCOVERY
   ?
  ADAPTIVE PLAN

  rule: AI does not blindly follow prior plan; new dependencies discovered during execution
  rule: graph changes require authority level check (see @../policies/evolution.sdd)

GraphVersion:
  PLAN-v1
   ?
  PLAN-v2

  v1: 8 tasks
  v2: 11 tasks
  reason: discovered ledger dependency

TaskGraphNode:
  structure:
    id: string (e.g. T1004)
    type: DISCOVERY | DESIGN | DECISION | IMPLEMENTATION | MIGRATION |
          TEST | REVIEW | DOCUMENTATION | VALIDATION | CLEANUP
    requires:
      - T1002
      - T1003
    produces:
      - RefundAPI
    consumes:
      - RefundAggregate
    consumes:
      - IdempotencyPattern
    conflicts:
      - none
    risk: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
    proof:
      - integration-test
    rollback:
      - revert-api-change
    touch:
      - payment/**

  TypedEdges:
    REQUIRES           — task cannot proceed without this dependency
    BLOCKS             — task blocks another from starting
    PRODUCES           — task produces an artifact/domain object
    CONSUMES           — task consumes an artifact/domain object
    CONFLICTS          — tasks conflict if run in parallel
    OPTIONAL_AFTER     — dependency optional once another task completes
    MUST_BE_BEFORE     — strict ordering constraint
    CAN_RUN_PARALLEL   — explicitly safe for parallel execution

  ResourceLock:
    mechanism: LOCK(scope)
    example:
      Task A touches: payment/service.go ? LOCK(payment/**)
      Task B touches: payment/service.go ? BLOCKED

  SemanticLock:
    mechanism: domain-level locking, not file-level
    example:
      @domain.Payment locked_by Agent-A
      Agent-B modifying Payment aggregate ? SEMANTIC_LOCK
    scope_hierarchy:
      payment (parent)
        ??? refund
        ??? settlement
        ??? balance
    rule: locking parent scope locks all child scopes
    rule: sibling sub-scopes (refund vs settlement) can run in parallel

TaskExecutionState:
  states:
    PENDING: not yet scheduled
    READY: dependencies satisfied, can be claimed
    CLAIMED: agent has claimed the task (with lease)
    RUNNING: actively being executed
    BLOCKED: waiting for dependency or decision
    WAITING_APPROVAL: risk CRITICAL, requires human approval
    VERIFYING: post-execution proof verification
    COMPLETED: all criteria met, proof verified
    FAILED: execution failed
    CANCELLED: abandoned or superseded

  Lease:
    duration: 30 min
    mechanism: heartbeat renewal
    expiration: LEASE_EXPIRED ? task returns to READY

  Rule: execution state is separate from task lifecycle phases
  (DISCOVERING, PLANNING, IMPLEMENTING, etc. in TaskLifecycle)

FailureRecovery:
  flow:
    FAIL
     ?
    CLASSIFY
     ?
    RETRY? / REPLAN? / ROLLBACK? / ESCALATE?

  Classification:
    CODE_FAILURE: code-level error
    TEST_FAILURE: test assertion failed
    CONTEXT_FAILURE: missing or incorrect context
    KNOWLEDGE_FAILURE: missing required knowledge
    DEPENDENCY_FAILURE: dependency unavailable
    ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE: runtime environment issue
    POLICY_FAILURE: policy/gate violation

  Action:
    CODE_FAILURE     ? analyze root cause, fix, retry (budget-limited)
    TEST_FAILURE     ? investigate: environment? test incorrect? code? (DO NOT blindly change code)
    CONTEXT_FAILURE  ? retrieve missing context, recompile, retry
    KNOWLEDGE_FAILURE ? initiate knowledge retrieval task
    DEPENDENCY_FAILURE ? wait for dependency, replan schedule
    ENVIRONMENT_FAILURE ? retry with backoff, escalate if persistent
    POLICY_FAILURE   ? escalate to human, do not auto-fix

RetryPolicy:
  max_attempts: 3
  rule: AI MUST describe WHAT CHANGED and WHY THIS ATTEMPT DIFFERS
  rule: if difference = none, retry is forbidden
  rule: after 3 failed attempts ? ESCALATE

  LoopDetection:
    pattern: T1 ? fail ? modify ? fail ? modify ? fail
    system: EXECUTION_LOOP_DETECTED
    action: stop retry, create investigation task

  ExecutionMemory:
    records:
      - previous attempts with outcomes
      - what was tried
      - what failed
      - what was learned

InvestigationTask:
  id_format: INV-NNN
  fields:
    problem: root cause description
    goal: identify root cause
    does_not_modify: production code (investigation only)
  flow:
    DISCOVERY
     ?
    ROOT_CAUSE
     ?
    PLAN_UPDATE

NegativeKnowledge:
  storage: @knowledge.negative
  example:
    DO_NOT: call repository from domain
    WHY: violates dependency boundary
    EVIDENCE: ARCH-FAIL-22

  principle: "knowing what NOT to do is often more valuable than knowing what to do"

FailurePatternLibrary:
  patterns:
    - @failure.circular-dependency
    - @failure.transaction-leak
    - @failure.duplicate-event
    - @failure.context-overload
    - @failure.unnecessary-abstraction

  usage: pre-loaded as preventive context before similar tasks

SelfHealingLoop:
  flow:
    PLAN
     ?
    CHECK
     ?
    EXECUTE
     ?
    VERIFY
     ?
    PROVE
     ?
    LEARN
     ?
    REPLAN
     ?
    NEXT TASK



  triggers:
    - research produces new decision
    - dependency invalidation
    - requirement change

  versioning:
    PLAN-100 v1:
      - T1
      - T2
      - T3

    PLAN-100 v2 (after research):
      - T1
      - T2
      - T3
      - T4

  rule: execution records which plan version was used
  rule: changes are audited via events

ResearchTask:
  definition: task whose output is a decision, not code

  example:
    TASK-RESEARCH-001:
      Goal: Evaluate Kafka vs RabbitMQ
      Output: ARCH-DECISION-001

  rule: research tasks MUST produce decision artifacts
  rule: research tasks MUST NOT produce source code

DecisionProducingTask:
  flow: Research -> Analysis -> Decision -> Implementation Tasks

  rule: decision MUST be recorded before implementation tasks proceed

TaskExecutionBoundary:
  rule: one execution = one task scope
  rule: agent MUST NOT switch tasks without formal TASK_SWITCH_REQUEST
  rule: files outside task scope are DENIED unless scope expansion is approved

ScopeBoundary:
  rule: task MUST define allowed and forbidden scopes
  rule: agent MUST NOT modify files outside task scope
  rule: scope expansion MUST go through formal request

ScopeExpansion:
  protocol:
    1. Agent detects need for out-of-scope change
    2. Agent creates SCOPE_EXPANSION_REQUEST
    3. Architect or human reviews request
    4. If approved: task scope is updated, new version created
    5. If denied: agent continues within original scope

TaskPriority:
  levels:
    - low
    - medium
    - high
    - critical

  rule: priority MUST NOT override blocking dependencies

TaskRisk:
  levels:
    - low
    - medium
    - high
    - critical

  mapping:
    low -> autonomous
    medium -> autonomous + review
    high -> approval required
    critical -> human required

TaskCheckpoint:
  definition: milestone where state snapshot is captured
  after_tasks: [list of task IDs]
  snapshot_includes:
    - CODE
    - TEST
    - PROOF
    - STATE
    - GRAPH
  rule: AI continues after checkpoint; does not need to stop after every task
  rule: checkpoint enables partial rollback boundary

PlanRevision:
  principle: Plan ? Contract
  plan: AI-generated, mutable, can change
  contract: immutable requirements, cannot violate
  rule: AI may revise plan based on discovery
  rule: AI may NOT revise requirements/contract

  revision_record:
    v1: 8 tasks
    v2: 11 tasks
    reason: discovered ledger dependency

Directories:
  active:
    path: ./active
    purpose: Currently executable tasks

  backlog:
    path: ./backlog
    purpose: Valid work not currently executable

  blocked:
    path: ./blocked
    purpose: Tasks waiting for dependency or decision

  review:
    path: ./review
    purpose: Tasks awaiting review or validation

  done:
    path: ./done
    purpose: Successfully completed tasks

  failed:
    path: ./failed
    purpose: Failed tasks requiring recovery

Rules:
  [T1] Tasks MUST be resolved from .sdd before execution.
  [T2] Task state MUST be updated after each stage.
  [T3] Blocked tasks MUST have explicit blockers.
  [T4] Completed tasks MUST be archived with outputs.
  [T5] Task graph MUST be a DAG — cycles are compile-time errors.
  [T6] Task MUST have exactly one primary goal.
  [T7] Task MUST have defined scope (allowed and forbidden).
  [T8] Task MUST have acceptance criteria.
  [T9] Task MUST declare dependencies and required skills.
  [T10] Task state is separate from execution state.
  [T11] AI proposes tasks; engine validates structure and constraints.
  [T12] Task decomposition MUST NOT be overly granular.
  [T13] Scope expansion MUST be formally requested and approved.
  [T14] Task coverage MUST map requirements to tasks and tests.
  [T15] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to task outputs.
  [T16] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in task output headers or titles.
  [T17] Every commit MUST reference linked DEC and TASK IDs in commit message.
  [T18] Branch naming: main -> stage -> test -> MODUL/<module> -> DEC/<id> -> TASK/<id>.
  [T19] Each task MUST have its own base branch derived from linked module branch.
  [T20] TASK branches are deleted after merge; DEC and MODUL branches persist.
  [T21] Only changed files are tested — full regression suites run on unchanged code only.
  [T22] Test execution MUST run inside Docker with resource limits enforced.

Navigation:
  Tasks: @tasks.sdd
  ProjectTasks: @../projects/{project_name}/tasks/INDEX.sdd
  Runtime: @../runtime/INDEX.sdd
  RuntimeMemoryModel: @../runtime/memory-model.sdd
  RuntimeContextBuilder: @../runtime/context-builder.sdd
  RuntimeContextPolicy: @../runtime/context-policy.sdd
  RuntimeContextManifest: @../runtime/context-manifest.sdd
  RuntimeConsolidation: @../runtime/memory-consolidation.sdd
  Orchestrator: @../orchestrator/INDEX.sdd
  Graph: @../graph/INDEX.sdd

State: +
